{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Vendor default credentials, as published in the vendors' own installation",
    "and administration documentation. These are factory settings, not stolen or",
    "leaked secrets: the finding this tool reports is that a device still answers",
    "to the password printed in its manual.",
    "",
    "Entries are ordered most-likely-first, because nwaa caps the number of",
    "attempts per login page (HARD_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_PAGE) and will only ever try",
    "the first few. This is a fingerprint-targeted default-credential check, not a",
    "password list: do not grow these lists into wordlists.",
    "",
    "An empty 'password' means the documented default is a blank password. An",
    "empty 'username' means the device authenticates with a PIN/password only.",
    "A profile with an empty 'credentials' list has no fixed factory default -",
    "that is a deliberate, documented entry, not an omission."
  ],
